# Milestone: M3 (activated at v0.13.3, refactor-3 SCHED-13)
# Covers: when all strands are on the sleep queue (none on the ready queue),
#         the VM is NOT quiescent — urbi_step reports WAKE_AT (timed work)
#         while the sleeper is parked; after the clock advances past the
#         deadline the sleeper resumes and finishes, and the step reports
#         QUIESCENT.  A further step stays QUIESCENT (idempotent verdict).
# matrix-row: scheduler-quiescent
#
# History: originally blocked on "a WAITING strand is intentionally counted
# in strand_runnable_count, so urbi_step returns RUNNING while any strand is
# parked" — gone under the single-writer runnable count (SCHED-01/B10, this
# arc's Task 1).  The lone-sleeper wake itself was fixed at v1.0/M10
# (design-risks v0.11.4-A: sched_wake_due_sleepers pre-dispatch pump).
# Activation closes the v1.0-loader-count-quiescence design-risk: vm_liveness
# (SCHED-13) is the one quiescence formula — sleepers are `timed` work
# (WAKE_AT), and a finished VM is QUIESCENT, with no phantom runnable count
# left behind by the park/wake cycle.
#
## host: realm sleeper
## host: run Realm.done = 0
## host: run sleep(100ms); Realm.done = 1
## host: run Realm.done
## host: step 5000
## host: advance-clock 200
## host: step 5000
## host: run Realm.done
## host: step 5000
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: WAKE_AT
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 1
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
